For my part, I decided to start playing nethack after having won
UofWashington's IMoria (mods to Moria 5.x) 6 times, and taking a 3 year
hiatus from "roguelike" (I still hate that term) games. I read the group for
long enough to figure out where to get the sources (without asking myself!
fancy that...), compiled everything, and read "Guidebook.ps" (after throwing
it at the appropriate magic marking device). This document informed me that
all the commands were different, and that I had a pet, and that I could eat
corpses. Sometimes. Not knowing anything else about the game, I figured "OK,
what the heck. I've won rogue, larn, and moria; how hard can nethack be?"
Needless to say, the Guidebook was pretty useless. So were the various help
items that I read. Sure, it's neat to know that such and such a creature came
form such and sucha mythos, but who cares? It doesn't tell me the stuff I
need to know, such as: "If you even think about messing with this monster if
you have less than 30000 hit points and a ACME Sword o Death, you're going to
get smeared". I got smeared. I still get smeared. My average high score is in
the middle thousands. I got lucky once; Somehow, I got 2 grateful nymphs from
a fountain, and picked up GDSM and SoR. What would I have wished for if I
hadn't read the spoilers? Probably a set of crystal plate mail, because I
happened to see that in a shop, and it looked good.

Yes, the Oracle will tell you stuff. However, in order to get the Oracle to
tell you anything, you need cash. LOTS of cash. Just where do you expect
someone to get 15K or so by the time they get to whatever level that is? You
blow your first 1000 or so, and the Oracle, in all her wisdom, tells you that
you can eat corpses. Thanks.

The complexity of nethack is such that, unlike moria or rogue, you *can't*
just sit down and expect to do well, or even close. The spoilers serve, IMHO,
to make the game *playable*, not "too easy". I think they should be cleaned
up and packaged with the sources.

Sorry for going on a tirade. The stress of my 3,001st death before 6th level
was getting to me...
